            <div xml:id="d506-a1">

                <pb facs="0365" n="293" xml:id="pg293"/>

                <p>At a public meeting held at the Free Trade Hall, Manchester, April 28, 1865, it
                    was moved by the Rev. G. W. Conder, seconded by Jacob Bright, esq,, and passed
                    unanimously—</p>
                <p>That the address of sympathy and condolence with Mrs. Lincoln, now read, be
                    adopted, and that the chairman be authorized to sign it on behalf of this
                    meeting.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FRANCIS TAYLOR,</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
